# gitleaks ignore file.
#
# One finding fingerprint per line: <file>:<rule-id>:<line>
# (e.g. `dashboard/src/utils.ts:aws-access-token:42`).
# A commit hash prefix (`<commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>`) is required to
# ignore findings in past commits / full-history scans.
#
# Prefer the inline `# gitleaks:allow` comment or an entry in .gitleaks.toml
# when the finding is a stable, repo-wide false positive; this file is for
# one-off or historical findings.
#
# Generate/refresh with: gitleaks baseline --source .
